<div class="editorial">
<header class="editorial-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Know Before You Go.</span><h1>Every Experience Matters.<br>Every Voice Counts.</h1><p class="lead">Every day, women navigate unfamiliar streets, neighbourhoods, workplaces and public spaces. Too often, those decisions come with limited information.</p><p>An uncomfortable encounter. An experience of harassment. A place someone avoids after dark. These experiences deserve to be heard, and the lessons they offer deserve to be shared.</p><div class="cta-row"><a class="button button-primary" href="<?= ps_escape(ps_url()) ?>">Explore the map <?= ps_icon('arrow-right') ?></a><a class="button button-secondary" href="<?= ps_escape(ps_url('#report')) ?>">Share an experience <?= ps_icon('plus') ?></a></div></header>
<section class="editorial-section"><h2>Turning Experiences<br>Into Awareness</h2><div><p>HerMap brings community-reported experiences together to help women understand patterns across India. Local awareness should be accessible, understandable and useful.</p><p>Reports are submitted without a public profile. After private review, eligible reports contribute to broad, delayed totals. Shared knowledge can help someone plan her next journey with more context.</p></div></section>
<section class="editorial-section"><h2>Her Voice.<br>Our Collective Awareness.</h2><div><p class="voice-line"><strong>Share an experience.</strong>Report without publicly revealing your identity. Selected report details are saved privately for review.</p><p class="voice-line"><strong>Explore your surroundings.</strong>Discover patterns of reported incidents across broad geographical areas.</p><p class="voice-line"><strong>Help someone else.</strong>Your experience may offer useful awareness to another woman visiting the same place.</p></div></section>
<section class="editorial-section"><h2>Built on Trust.<br>Guided by Responsibility.</h2><div><p>A report is an experience shared, not a proven finding of wrongdoing. An area with fewer reports is not necessarily safer, and more reports do not define everyone who lives or works there.</p><p>HerMap communicates the information alongside its limits. We encourage informed choices, care for one another and responsible reporting.</p><a class="text-link" href="<?= ps_escape(ps_url('how-it-works')) ?>">Understand how HerMap works <?= ps_icon('arrow-right') ?></a></div></section>
<section class="editorial-section"><h2>By the Community.<br>For the Community.</h2><div><p>Access to information about personal safety should be available to everyone. HerMap is free to explore and free to contribute to. Reporting will always be free.</p><p>Informed choices begin with shared awareness.</p></div></section>
<section class="editorial-cta"><span class="eyebrow">Our shared mission</span><h2><?= ps_campaign() ?></h2><p>Every experience shared with care could help another woman make an informed choice.</p><div class="cta-row"><a class="button button-primary" href="<?= ps_escape(ps_url('#report')) ?>">Share an experience <?= ps_icon('plus') ?></a><a class="button button-secondary" href="<?= ps_escape(ps_url()) ?>">Explore the map <?= ps_icon('map') ?></a></div></section>
